<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Evaluation</h2>

<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Experimental Settings</h3>

<section id="S4.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.1.1 </span>Dataset</h4>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To verify the effectiveness of <span id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Patient-Zero</span> in constructing and simulating patients, we followed existing research practices <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al. (2024a)</a></cite> by randomly selecting six medical departments with common diseases from a department and disease list. Finally, the following medical departments are adopted: Psychiatry, Urology, Orthopedics, Ophthalmology, Endocrinology, and General Surgery, and for each department we generated 10,000 synthetic patient records. The knowledge base used to generate the patient records is derived from the Baidu Health Encyclopedia<span id="footnote3" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">3</span>
                
                
                
              <a href="https://jiankang.baidu.com/" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://jiankang.baidu.com/</a></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For the selected diseases, demographic data including gender and age, were estimated based on typical medical practices. Gender was evenly distributed for general conditions, while gender-specific conditions were assigned accordingly. Age was categorized into three groups: children (0-17), adults (18-59), and elderly (60-85), covering a broad range of medical concerns.
Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Synthetic Patient Record ‣ Patient-Zero: A Unified Framework for Real-Record-Free Patient Agent Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a> shows an example of the generated record.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.1.2 </span>Evaluation Metrics</h4>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The quality of synthetic medical records is typically assessed through quantitative metrics to ensure the generated data are accurate and sufficiently diverse, so <span id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">accuracy</span> and <span id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">diversity</span> related metrics are adopted: 1)
Accuracy is formulated as the ratio of the number of patient records that are precisely aligned with medical standards to the total number of patient records, which is calculated by
Hippomistral-7B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Acikgoz et al. (2024)</a></cite> with CoT in Table <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 4.1.3 Baselines and Implementation Details ‣ 4.1 Experimental Settings ‣ 4 Evaluation ‣ Patient-Zero: A Unified Framework for Real-Record-Free Patient Agent Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
2) Diversity is evaluated using metrics such as BLEU, ROUGE-L, and Cosine Similarity with default parameters.
We use BERTScore <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al. (2020)</a></cite> and GPTScore <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fu et al. (2024)</a></cite> to measure the semantic similarity of synthetic patient record datatext <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gao et al. (2024)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For the conversation ability of the generated patient agents, we focus on three core dimensions:
<span id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dialogue consistency</span> measures the extent to which the patient agent’s responses align with the generated patient record. <span id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Emotional consistency</span> and <span id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">conversational fluency</span> are each rated on a 7-point scale by GPT-4o. The former metric evaluates the consistency of emotional expressions to the predefined patient features, while the latter assesses the naturalness and fluidity of the language used.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.1.3 </span>Baselines and Implementation Details</h4>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compare our <span id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Patient-Zero</span> framework with existing baselines that generate synthetic patient records using real medical data.
LDP-GAN <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gwon et al. (2024)</a></cite> generates synthetic patient medical records by using GANs and local differential privacy (LDP), adding noise to the synthetic data to protect individual privacy.
Synthea <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Walonoski et al. (2017)</a></cite> simulates realistic medical histories and health records using publicly available health statistics and clinical guidelines.
The Avatar method <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guillaudeux et al. (2023)</a></cite> generates synthetic data by using a patient-centered approach to create a local random simulation for each original observation.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T1" class="ltx_table">
<div id="S4.T1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:73.2pt;vertical-align:-33.6pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(28.2pt,-6.0pt) scale(1.1955269894742,1.1955269894742) ;">
<table id="S4.T1.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S4.T1.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T1.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Method</span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T1.2.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Accuracy</span> <math id="S4.T1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T1.2.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">BERTScore</span> <math id="S4.T1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T1.2.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GPTScore</span> <math id="S4.T1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T1.2.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">AVATAR</td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">95.00%</td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.9639</td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.4766</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T1.2.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">LDP-GAN</td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">86.00%</td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.9529</td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.3488</td></tr>
