<td id="S4.T1.2.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.9243</td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.4340</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T1.2.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">Patient-Zero</td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S4.T1.2.1.5.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">100.00%</span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S4.T1.2.1.5.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.8637</span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S4.T1.2.1.5.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.2389</span></td></tr>
</table>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>Performance comparison of baseline models against Patient-Zero, outperforming all baselines in accuracy and diversity. The accuracy of the data is measured on 100 synthetic patients using the open-source medical LLM, Hippomistral-7B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Acikgoz et al. (2024)</a></cite>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To verify the flexibility of our <span id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Patient-Zero</span>, we use four distinct LLMs, namely Doubao (Doubao-pro-32k), GPT-3.5 (gpt-3.5-turbo-1106), GPT-4o-mini (gpt-4o-mini), and GPT-4o (gpt-4o-2024-08-06), to generate medical records in all experiments. The temperature is set to 1.0, with maximum tokens of 4,096 to limit response length.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Performance of Generated Records</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate the accuracy of our generated data using various LLMs based on the Disease Knowledge Base, comparing results across different departments in Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.2 Performance of Generated Records ‣ 4 Evaluation ‣ Patient-Zero: A Unified Framework for Real-Record-Free Patient Agent Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. This includes general-purpose LLMs like GPT-4o, Gemini-2, and Grok-3, as well as open-source medical LLMs such as Hippomistral-7B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Acikgoz et al. (2024)</a></cite> and Llama3-OpenBioLLM-8B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ankit Pal (2024)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
